          "heading": "Jake White's 35-man Fiji squad includes ex-England Nathan Hughes, four uncapped players",
          "body": "Ex-England back Nathan Hughes, who won 22 caps between 2016 and 2019, is in Fiji's squad after being drafted into Jake White's 35-man group for the November Nations Championship block. He is one of four uncapped players, alongside Peniami Narisia, Marika Parker and Setareki Bituniyata, and White could give the other three their first Test caps this month. Fiji come in off a 34-28 win over Japan and face France, Ireland and Italy."
